# Live Entry Radar evaluator cadence. systemd calendars have no ET, so the window
# is expressed as the UTC SPAN that covers 09:2x-16:2x ET (session window + cron
# grace) in BOTH DST regimes — 13:2xZ..20:2xZ under EDT, 14:2xZ..21:2xZ under EST —
# and the pass itself stands down on the EASTERN clock via
# engine/entry_radar/live_eval.py's in_window (which also consults the NYSE
# calendar, so holidays cost nothing). One schedule, one window definition, no
# second copy of "when is the market open".
#
# The ~24 out-of-window ticks a day are a Python start that exits at in_window and
# publishes health.state="out_of_window"; the cost of getting a UTC-pinned window
# wrong is a dark hour every session for five months of the year.
#
# :04/5 IS A WRITER-RACE OFFSET, and the three-way spacing is the point:
#   :00/5   macro-live-snapshot fires on the 5-minute boundary and takes up to
#           ~230 s to publish the full-universe quote file;
#   :03/5   macro-live-prophet reads it three minutes later;
#   :04/5   this lane, one minute behind Prophet.
# This lane reads the SAME quote artifacts Prophet does (design §3b: state/
# quotes_full.json + the live/quotes.json overlay, freshest-wins) and must not race
# the writer — four minutes of head start is the difference between reading this
# cycle's snapshot and the previous one. Publication is an atomic rename either
# way, so a read is never partial; the offset buys CURRENCY, not safety. The extra
# minute past Prophet is also cheap separation on a 2-vCPU box: two capped oneshots
# that both wake on the same second contend for the same cores for nothing.
#
# Persistent=false — a missed pass is a missed 5-minute interval, and replaying it
# later would evaluate a stale tape against a live clock. The next tick is the
# recovery; health.pass.prev_gap_intervals is how the gap is reported.
[Unit]
Description=Run the Live Entry Radar evaluator every five minutes across the US session

[Timer]
OnCalendar=Mon..Fri *-*-* 13..21:04/5:00 UTC
AccuracySec=1s
RandomizedDelaySec=10s
Persistent=false
Unit=macro-live-entry-radar.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
